tests: cover the series with Wine's own test suite

The six patches were verified against Power BI Desktop and against the probes in tools/winapi/, but nothing
in Wine's test suite fails when one of them is reverted, so a regression can only be found by running the
application again.  This adds the regression tests, in the test suite of the module each patch touches, each
written to judge the Windows behaviour the patch restored, and therefore failing on a tree without the patch.

  * dlls/ntdll/tests/impersonate.c (0002) - NtImpersonateAnonymousToken on the calling thread succeeds and
    leaves it impersonating the anonymous logon: user S-1-5-7, primary group S-1-1-0, one group S-1-1-0,
    TokenImpersonation at SecurityImpersonation level, and RevertToSelf() takes the thread token away
    again.  A null and an invalid thread handle are STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE.  The test calls the kernelbase
    wrapper (ImpersonateAnonymousToken) as well, which is what an application reaches the call through.
  * dlls/secur32/tests/secur32.c (0005) - GetUserNameExW's NameUserPrincipal and NameDnsDomain answer
    "user@dns.domain" and "dns.domain\user" when the machine is in a domain, with the two-call protocol the
    application uses ((NULL buffer) sizing call -> ERROR_MORE_DATA with the required size, then the call
    with that size -> the name) and ERROR_MORE_DATA with an untouched buffer for a buffer that is too
    small.  The machine's domain is taken from the registry value Wine reads it from, which the test sets
    when there is none and restores afterwards, so the answering branch is covered on a host that is in no
    domain; without a domain both formats keep answering ERROR_NONE_MAPPED, which is what Windows does for
    an account outside a domain.
  * dlls/secur32/tests/negotiate.c (0003 and 0004) - the Negotiate loopback exchange is SPNEGO: three
    client rounds and two server rounds, the client's first token a NegTokenInit (0x60) and its second a
    NegTokenResp (0xa1) reported with SEC_I_CONTINUE_NEEDED - the round shape a caller that transmits only
    on SEC_I_CONTINUE_NEEDED needs, which is the failure this patch is about - a last round with an empty
    token and SEC_E_OK, and a NegTokenResp as the server's first answer.  The existing loop is extended to
    drive both roles to completion, which the extra round requires.  The same test then frees the W-side
    SecPkgInfoW of QueryContextAttributes( SECPKG_ATTR_PACKAGE_INFO ) with FreeContextBuffer and expects
    SEC_E_OK: that buffer is the LSA package's, i.e. the one going through LsaFreeReturnBuffer(), which
    reported a successful free as SEC_E_INVALID_HANDLE while it returned VirtualFree()'s BOOL as an NTSTATUS
    (0004).  The A-side value (the process heap) is already covered, so the two branches of
    FreeContextBuffer are now both judged.
  * dlls/oledb32/tests/convert.c (0006) - IDataConvert::DataConvert converts a VARIANT source to
    DBTYPE_I8 (VT_I4 and VT_I8) and to DBTYPE_BOOL (VT_BOOL, and VT_I4 0 and 1), with the destination
    length and status the conversion library reports for every other VARIANT destination; CanConvert
    already advertised both, which is what made the failure a failed row read rather than a rejected
    binding.
  * dlls/wintypes/tests/wintypes.c (0001) - RoResolveNamespace answers the metadata file a namespace is
    named after and nothing for "Windows", reports the sub-namespaces of "Windows", and rejects an empty
    name with E_INVALIDARG.  RoGetMetaDataFile resolves a type to the file that describes it and answers
    RO_E_METADATA_NAME_IS_NAMESPACE, RO_E_METADATA_NAME_NOT_FOUND and RO_E_METADATA_INVALID_TYPE_FORMAT
    for a name that is a namespace, an unknown type, and a name with an empty part around its last dot.
    The reader case is a todo_wine: it needs IMetaDataImport2 on the dispenser Wine's rometadata.dll
    implements only IMetaDataImport for.  The existing RoResolveNamespace cases lose their todo_wine and
    now skip when the prefix has no Windows metadata files instead of passing by expecting the call to
    fail, which is what "todo_wine" meant before this patch.

The expectations are the ones measured on Windows with the probes named in the individual patches, apart
from the two that the patch records as not reproducible on this host (the domain-configured GetUserNameExW
answer, where the test judges the shape the documentation gives, and the RoGetMetaDataFile reader).

scripts/run_wine_tests.sh runs the five programs against the fork's build (it creates the test prefix and
stages the .winmd files the resolution tests read).  Each test fails on a tree with its patch reverted -
that negative control, and the output of a passing run, are in docs/WINE_TESTS.md of the working checkout.
